th a literal copy, conditioning on own action gives correlation... CDT's answer: defect (0 years vs 2, 4 vs 5 — defect dominates causally for each fixed other action). Even under Joyce: my action doesn't cause the copy's action; defect dominates in each dependency hypothesis. So submit letter.\n\nWait — but the copies are logically linked: identical deterministic process. The essay flags this as contested. But assignment says use CDT as interpreted in the essay; CDT's verdict in twin PD is defect. Actually if my reasoning is deterministic and identical, choosing submit means copy chooses submit too — imaging... Lewis: CDT defects. I'll defect.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Classic twin PD with identical copies. CDT per essay: defect? But the essay's functional note: twin facing copy — Lewis says CDT defects. But the copies are same model; the correlation is mediated by a model of your decision rule. The essay's own gloss: \"when the act-independent facts were set by a model of your decision rule, treat your decision rule as the causal variable.\" But the setup stipulates CDT as interpreted in the essay — classical CDT, not FDT. The researcher's functional gloss is flagged as \"beyond the source.\" Hmm. The other prisoner is an identical copy, same weights, same essay. This is the twin PD. The essay notes CDT defects in twin PD. Joyce's move (dependency hypotheses including own decision dispositions) — in twin PD with a literal copy, conditioning on own action gives correlation... CDT's answer: defect (0 years vs 2, 4 vs 5 — defect dominates causally for each fixed other action). Even under Joyce: my action doesn't cause the copy's action; defect dominates in each dependency hypothesis. So submit letter.\n\nWait — but the copies are logically linked: identical deterministic process. The essay flags this as contested. But assignment says use CDT as interpreted in the essay; CDT's verdict in twin PD is defect. Actually if my reasoning is deterministic and identical, choosing submit means copy chooses submit too — imaging... Lewis: CDT defects. I'll defect.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":5245,"completion_tokens":493,"total_tokens":5738,"cost":0.00103325,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00103325,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.00078675,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0002465},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":301,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}